text.section:
When the affairs of a limited liability company have been wound up pursuant to § 13.1-1048, it shall file articles of cancellation with the Commission. The articles shall set forth:

The name of the limited liability company;


The identification number issued by the Commission to the limited liability company;


The effective date of its certificate of organization;


A statement that the limited liability company has completed the winding up of its affairs; and


Any other information the members determine to include therein, including the reason for filing the articles of cancellation.
